# Compile-only smoke test corpus: tests/cmm-fail/<name>.c-- sources that are
# INTENTIONAL negative tests - upstream wrote them to be rejected by the
# compiler, and the point of the test is that they fail with a specific
# diagnostic. See cmm-pass.tests's header for why this manifest exists
# alongside the directory split (belt-and-suspenders, not the source of
# truth).
#
# Every name here must have a golden diagnostic at cmm-fail/output/<name>.s2
# (recorded/refreshed via run-compile.sh --update). Unlike cmm-pass.tests,
# there is no "known gap" escape hatch: a name here that starts compiling
# successfully is never expected, and run-compile.sh reports it as a
# regression (the compiler silently accepting something it used to reject).
#
# One name per line, no extension, no directory (always tests/cmm-fail/<name>.c--).

badlit8
err-000
err-001
err-002
exp-002
exp-003
non-local-cut
test-000
test-001
test-002
